module gunbc.stage0_emit_model

import gunbc.generated_artifact { committed_generated_artifact_paths }
import gunbc.stage0_emit_plan { stage0_canonical_repo_path, stage0_module_emit_basename, stage0_module_emit_filename }

data stage0_generated_membership_grounding_note: String = "MEMBERSHIP IS ASKED OF THE GENERATED-ARTIFACT REGISTRY, NOT OF A ROSTER. This module formerly read gunbc.stage0_emit_plan_generated.committed_generated_stage0_artifact_files — a 142-entry hand-shaped list that regen_stage0 re-authored on every heal. The v1 cut deleted the src/v1 .dag authority and the regen loop, so that roster had no producer; running the heal against the cut tree re-authored it as a two-entry husk, which is the regrowth trap (a corpse re-grown by the loop that was supposed to die with it). PROVENANCE, ADDED 2026-08-16 BECAUSE THIS SENTENCE CARRIED NONE: the two-entry figure was MEASURED, by me, by running generated_artifact_gate main_wet on integration/v1-cut at an EARLIER POINT IN THIS CUT than the tree you are reading. Re-measured on the same branch after later commits restored swept test fixtures, the same regeneration yields SEVEN entries (compiler_tests, lib, v1_rt, v1_test_non_ascii_perf_fixture, wt_a, wt_b, wt_common). Both numbers are true of the trees they were taken on and neither is a property of the mechanism. THE CONCLUSION THIS SENTENCE DREW WAS ALSO SUPERSEDED: 'the roster and its artifact variant are retired whole' was reversed by operator ruling the same night -- the authority gunbc.stage0_emit_plan was never deleted, only its projection, its renderer and the registry hookup were, so the correct action was to restore the generation path and REGENERATE rather than to retire. That is done. This paragraph is kept rather than rewritten because a conclusion with no tree and no date is indistinguishable from a measurement to the next reader, and it nearly was to its own author four hours later.

WHAT REPLACES IT IS NOT A SHORTER LIST. The question 'is this stage0 .rs generated' has exactly one honest answer post-cut: a file is generated if and only if something can still re-derive it, and the single authority for that is gunbc.generated_artifact — so membership is now a lookup in committed_generated_artifact_paths() at the canonical stage0 path, with no second representation to drift against. The population it returns is therefore SMALL and derived rather than large and asserted: the stage0 .rs that remain registry artifacts in their own right, and nothing else. Every other file under src/v1/stage0/src is frozen hand-owned seed source, which is precisely what the freeze means and what the sibling lanes deleting hand Rust there are acting on. TWO SENSES OF GENERATED NOW COLLIDE ON ONE FILE, AND THE GUARD THAT WOULD HAVE SAID SO WAS DELETED BY THIS SAME CUT. The deleted regen_stage0 carried assert_registry_is_partitioned, which refused if any member of committed_generated_stage0_artifact_files() also appeared in HAND_MAINTAINED_STAGE0_FILES. Measured on this branch: committed_generated_stage0_artifact_files() returns bootstrap_stage0_crate_layout_generated.rs and v1_interpreter_dispatch_generated.rs, and the hand roster contains the second of those — so the assert would REFUSE here, and it is gone. THE CAUSE IS A SUBJECT CHANGE, NOT A NEW OVERLAP: at the fork base this function answered (which files does regen_stage0 emit), and it now answers (which stage0 paths are committed generated artifacts). Those are different questions, and the hand roster is written in a THIRD sense — v2.compiler.self_host.frontier hand_maintained_stage0_filenames means NOT SELF-EMITTED BY THE v2 FRONTIER, which a gunbc-produced artifact can be while still being generated. So the collision is a §3 nickname defect between three readings of one word, exposed rather than created by the re-home. WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED: that anything is broken today. No surviving consumer joins these two rosters — the only one did, and this cut deleted it — so the overlap is currently unobserved rather than harmful, and restoring the assert would mean investing in frozen Rust whose host binary no longer exists. Recorded here as a declared rung drop with its measurement, rather than left for whoever next assumes the two rosters partition.

The prior fork this dissolves is recorded on gunbc.roster_registry, which had already caught the roster drifting 98 against the Rust const's 101 and named 'regen_stage0 reads the .dag rows and the const is deleted' as the close. The fork closes here by the other end: the reader is deleted."

fn is_committed_generated_stage0_artifact(basename: String) -> Bool {
  any(
    committed_generated_artifact_paths(),
    path => path == stage0_canonical_repo_path(basename: basename)
  )
}

data stage0_src_repo_prefix: String = "src/v1/stage0/src/"

fn committed_generated_stage0_artifact_files() -> List<String> {
  committed_generated_artifact_paths()
    |> filter(path => starts_with(s: path, prefix: stage0_src_repo_prefix))
    |> map(path => replace(path, stage0_src_repo_prefix, ""))
}

fn committed_generated_stage0_artifact_count() -> Int {
  length(committed_generated_stage0_artifact_files())
}
